  "notes": "University Park. Major code 'ENGY' avoids colliding with the EGEE department prefix. The 'EGEE 451 or ENVSE 470' item lists EGEE 451 first per the bulletin's own ordering, but EGEE 451 needs FSC 431 (a Fuel Science course not otherwise part of this plan) — relies on the engine's option-fallback fix to resolve to ENVSE 470 instead, whose own prerequisite (MATH 251) is already satisfied earlier in this plan. Handbook-verification pass (2026-08-26): the department's real, current (Spring 2024+) approved-electives page (eme.psu.edu/undergraduate/academics/undergraduate-programs/energy-engineering-major/eneng-approved-electives-0) names an exact course list for all five elective categories -- 'Material Science elective', 'Fuel Science elective', 'Professional elective', 'Technical elective', and 'Energy Systems elective' -- previously modeled as bare unfillable placeholders. Wired each via a match regex using only the codes still present in this app's scraped catalogs; dropped ENGR 312, AE 456, ME 402, and PNG 405 (no longer exist in the current catalog) and corrected ENVSE 404 and ESC 414 to their real current codes (ENVSE 404W, ESC 414M). Post-scraper-fix repair: CHEM 110's real prereq is MATH 22, which was never in this plan at all -- and MATH 22 itself real-chains through MATH 21, MATH 4, and MATH 3, none of which were in the plan either, leaving CHEM 110 (and everything chained off CHEM 112/202/EME 301/EGEE 302/304/437/430/411W) permanently unschedulable. Added all four (MATH 3, MATH 4, MATH 21, MATH 22) as explicit items; confirmed clean (no warnings, goal met) after the addition -- this plan's larger 19cr/semester cap gave enough room to absorb the extra 12cr without a 9th term, unlike EET/EMET which needed slot-conversion tricks to stay within an 18cr cap.",
